    <!-- Short answer -->
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="answer-heading">
      <h2 id="answer-heading">Can You Get Temporary Alimony in the UAE? The Short Answer</h2>
      <p>
        Yes, if you ask for it and the court agrees. Temporary alimony, also called interim maintenance,
        temporary spousal maintenance or temporary spousal support, is a short-term order that makes the paying spouse cover the basic costs
        of the wife and children while the court works out the final figures. How you get it depends on
        which family law governs your marriage.
      </p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Muslim couples, and others under Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024:</strong> Article 100 lets the court, during the hearings of an alimony case and at the wife’s request, order temporary alimony for her and her children, enforceable immediately by force of law.</li>
        <li><strong>Non-Muslims under Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2022:</strong> alimony is claimed after the divorce judgment (Article 9), and the executive regulation lets the divorced wife ask for temporary alimony until her financial rights are decided.</li>
        <li><strong>Non-Muslims at the Abu Dhabi Civil Family Court:</strong> under Abu Dhabi Law No. 14 of 2021 and its 2022 Regulation, a divorced woman can ask for provisional alimony by interim order (Article 21), and any interested party can seek a provisional order on temporary alimony or housing (Article 42).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In every track the word that matters is &ldquo;may&rdquo;: the court is allowed to order temporary
        alimony, not obliged to. This page covers only that interim period. For what the final judgment can
        award, see our main guide to <a href="/en/alimony-uae/">alimony in the UAE</a>.
      </p>
